{"name":"Weeping Fig","hex":"#5d8727","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weeping fig","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ornamental tree of species Ficus benjamina, often grown in containers indoors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weeping_fig"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ficus benjamina","blocks":[{"text":"Ficus benjamina, commonly known as weeping fig, benjamin fig or ficus tree and often sold in stores as just ficus, is a species of flowering plant in the family Moraceae, native to Asia and Australia. It is the official tree of Bangkok. The species is also naturalized in the West Indies and in the states of Florida and Arizona in the United States. Its small fruit are favored by some birds. Ficus trees have proved to have environmental benefits in urban areas, such as acting as biomonitors. The species is also associated with some allergens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Starr-080608-7576-Ficus_benjamina-habit_with_Laysan_albatross-Gym_Sand_Island-Midway_Atoll_%2824823189861%29.jpg/330px-Starr-080608-7576-Ficus_benjamina-habit_with_Laysan_albatross-Gym_Sand_Island-Midway_Atoll_%2824823189861%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ficus_benjamina"},{"title":"Fig","blocks":[{"text":"The fig is the edible fruit of Ficus carica, a species of tree or shrub in the flowering plant family Moraceae, native to the Mediterranean region, and to western and southern Asia. It has been cultivated since ancient times and is now widely grown throughout the world. Ficus carica is the type species of the genus Ficus, which comprises over 800 tropical and subtropical plant species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg/330px-Ficus_carica_L%2C_1771.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fig"}],"ima